---
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import BaseLayout from "../../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { projects } from "../../data/projects";

const project = projects.find((item) => item.href === "/projects/ink/")!;
---
<BaseLayout title="INK" description={project.description} work={{ type: "CreativeWork" }}>
  <header class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Project / Credential &amp; evidence management</p>
    <h1>INK</h1>
    <p class="lead">Keep what the terminal forgets. An encrypted, local-first credential and authentication-evidence notebook for penetration testing engagements and training labs.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button button-primary" href={project.repository}>View source on GitHub <Icon name="lucide:arrow-up-right" /></a>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/projects/">All projects</a>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="container section content-layout">
    <figure class="project-flow">
      <ol>
        <li>Create a passphrase-encrypted notebook</li>
        <li>Record identities, secrets, and provenance</li>
        <li>Track authentication results and reuse evidence</li>
        <li>Review and export an offline report</li>
      </ol>
      <figcaption>INK’s capture-to-report workflow. Each engagement has its own local notebook.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The problem</h2>
      <p>An assessment can produce credentials, hashes, service accounts, reused passwords, and partial access observations across dozens of terminals and hosts. Without a consistent record, it becomes difficult to answer where a credential came from, which service accepted it, or what was actually verified.</p>

      <h2>Capture and provenance</h2>
      <p>INK is a Python command-line tool that stores identities, passwords, hashes, tokens, domains, hosts, services, and source information together. Operators can append timestamped notes and validation results, search metadata, edit entries, and import records from CSV. Bulk entry supports multiple user-secret pairs without saving incomplete batches.</p>
      <p>INK records observed access; it does not automatically attempt authentication or test credentials.</p>

      <h2>Encrypted, local-first storage</h2>
      <p>Each assessment uses a separate SQLite notebook protected by a master passphrase. Record payloads are encrypted using Fernet, with keys derived through scrypt and a per-notebook salt. Secret entry uses hidden terminal prompts, and ordinary listing commands keep secrets masked. There is no cloud account, API server, telemetry, or background service.</p>

      <h2>Review and HTML export</h2>
      <p>INK produces a self-contained HTML report with search, filters, record timelines, reveal and copy controls, CSV download, and printable layouts. By default, a successful export clears the selected notebook after the report is written and verified. The <code>--keep</code> option retains the notebook for subsequent work.</p>
      <p><strong>Important:</strong> exported HTML and downloaded CSV reports contain plaintext secrets even when the report masks them on screen. These reports are private assessment artifacts, not files for public repositories.</p>

      <h2>Example workflow</h2>
      <p>Create an assessment notebook with <code>ink new assessment</code>, add a record with <code>ink add assessment</code>, log validation using <code>ink validate assessment 1</code>, and generate a non-destructive report with <code>ink export assessment --output assessment.html --keep</code>.</p>

      <h2>Design boundaries</h2>
      <p>INK is a lightweight personal notebook rather than a network scanner or a fully audited password manager. The encryption cannot protect an unlocked session, compromised machine, or clipboard contents. The repository includes fictional demonstration data and automated tests; operational records stay local.</p>

      <div class="tag-list">{project.stack.map((tag) => <span class="tag">{tag}</span>)}</div>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={project.repository + "/blob/main/README.md"}>Installation and documentation <Icon name="lucide:arrow-up-right" /></a>
        <a class="text-link" href={project.repository + "/blob/main/examples/Revachol.html"}>Example report <Icon name="lucide:arrow-up-right" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
